;; Larry Koopa's airship cabin (0.5.0, SMB3 style, after the owner's reference of SMB3's cabin and
;; the SMB3 art's mock of it): enclosed, no sky. The log back wall (`H`, not solid) fills the room,
;; with two porthole windows; a ceiling of beams across row 2 and a pillar down each edge column
;; (smb3 decor, 16x16, one per tile, drawn over solid `%` so the room stays closed); a floor of log
;; posts, `#` the post tops on row 13 and `%` the posts carrying on below, and one raised post at
;; (7,12). The airship deck's stern pipe (`4-2-airship`) leads here (`4-2-larry 2 12`): as in
;; SMB3, the hero drops in out of a pipe hanging from the ceiling at the left (`smb3:ceiling-pipe`,
;; drawn over the players so he comes out of it; the ceiling is open over column 2, the shaft he
;; falls down, centred under the pipe's mouth). Larry hops at the
;; hero, fires wand blasts and spins in his shell when stomped; beaten, he drops the crystal ball,
;; whose touch is 4-2's secret exit `secret:larry` (docs/HEROES.md).
[tiles]
;; Rows 0-1 stay clear (no tiles, black): the SMB3 status bar draws the world 32 px up, so they sit
;; off the top of the screen, where the hero's drop starts. The room's ceiling starts on row 2.
